{
  "_doc": [
    "All matching is case-insensitive and typo-tolerant (see pipeline/keywords.py).",
    "Text and keywords are normalised the same way first: lowercase, 'A.I.'->'ai', 'M.o.U'->'mou',",
    "hyphens/slashes -> spaces, center->centre, program->programme, -ize->-ise.",
    "A trailing * is a prefix match: 'allocat*' = allocate/allocated/allocation.",
    "Words of 6+ letters also match misspellings (same first letter, similarity >= 0.88):",
    "'artifical inteligence', 'goverment', 'minster', 'memorandam' all match.",
    "Short words (ai, mou, cm, rfp) are exact only - fuzzy matching them causes false hits.",
    "mask_phrases are removed from the text before government/central matching, so a bare 'state' or 'Centre' can be a keyword without 'state-of-the-art' or 'data centre' triggering it.",
    "gov_terms includes state leaders/bodies (names change after elections - keep this list current)."
